+// Frame GPU time without a GL query (KL_MTL_FRAME_GPU_TIME=1). ContextMtl::flush()
+// (= the guest's glFlush, one per frame) closes the running TimeElapsed entry and
+// opens the next one; the entry machinery already sums GPUEndTime-GPUStartTime over
+// every command buffer created meanwhile. Completed frames are queued here and
+// popped by the host via ANGLEMetalPopFrameGpuTimeMs(). Needed where a live
+// GL_TIME_ELAPSED query is forbidden (OVR_multiview draws) and for a measurement
+// that is identical before and after such a change. Mutually exclusive with GL
+// TimeElapsed queries (both drive CommandQueue's single active entry).
+bool FrameGpuTimeEnabled();
+void PushFrameGpuTimeMs(double ms);
